;; Go-build variant of java.nio.channels.spi.AbstractInterruptibleChannel (J2G-SPEC §4.6;
;; doc/classes/JAVA-DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, F7, "As built: F7 (write-ahead)"; JCS162 (a), "As built: JCS162"):
;; read by j2g only. jdk26u registers the channel's (and AbstractSelector's) Interruptible with the
;; thread through SharedSecrets' JavaLangAccess.blockedOn, which jrt has not: here blockedOn calls jrt's
;; Thread directly (jdk.internal.jrt.HostThreads.blockedOn, go/arbace/jrt/thread.ae), whose interrupt
;; calls the blocker's interrupt(Thread) and postInterrupt as jdk26u's Thread.interrupt does, so that an
;; interrupt closes a channel a thread is blocked on (ClosedByInterruptException) and wakes a selector.
;; begin and end are jdk26u's (baf63fb). Copyright (c) the Arbace authors; Eclipse Public License 1.0.
(in-ns 'java.nio.channels.spi)

(j2g/variant AbstractInterruptibleChannel
  (method ^:static blockedOn ^void [^Interruptible intr]
    (jdk.internal.jrt.HostThreads/blockedOn intr)))
